# Linesform Studio — configuration reference
#
# Copy to .env.local for local development (git-ignored), and set the same
# names in your hosting provider's environment settings for deployments.
# Never put real secrets in this file. This is a single Next.js application:
# there is no separate backend, so every variable lives here. NEXT_PUBLIC_*
# values are embedded in the browser bundle at BUILD time — they are public by
# design and must never hold secrets. All other values stay on the server.
# See docs/analytics-and-seo.md for the full setup, including dashboards.

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Site
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

# SITE_URL — canonical production origin, e.g. https://www.example.com (no trailing slash).
#   Used for: canonical tags, Open Graph URLs, sitemap.xml, robots.txt, structured data.
#   Required for production. Public (not a secret). Server/build configuration.
#   Get it from: your domain / hosting provider. Read at build time — rebuild after changing.
#   If unset: on Vercel the project's production domain is used automatically;
#   elsewhere a production build publishes NO canonical URLs and an EMPTY sitemap
#   (and warns during the build). Development falls back to http://localhost:3000.
SITE_URL=

# GOOGLE_SITE_VERIFICATION — Google Search Console "HTML tag" verification token
#   (only the content value, not the whole <meta> tag).
#   Optional: only needed if you verify with the HTML-tag method. Public (it appears
#   in the page source). Server/build configuration. Not a tracking ID — unrelated to GTM.
#   Get it from: Search Console → Add property → URL prefix → HTML tag.
GOOGLE_SITE_VERIFICATION=

# CONTACT_EMAIL — public contact address shown in the footer, the contact section,
#   the contact assistant and the legal pages.
#   Optional. Public. Server/build configuration. If unset, no address is shown anywhere
#   and the legal pages say that none has been published.
CONTACT_EMAIL=

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Tracking (Google Tag Manager)
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

# NEXT_PUBLIC_GTM_ID — Google Tag Manager web container ID, e.g. GTM-XXXXXXX.
#   Optional. Public by design (it is visible in the page). Frontend, read at BUILD time.
#   Get it from: tagmanager.google.com → your container → the ID shown next to its name.
#   If unset or malformed: GTM is never loaded, the cookie banner is not shown (there
#   are no optional cookies) and the cookie policy says so.
#   GA4, Google Ads and Meta Pixel IDs are NOT environment variables: they are
#   configured as tags inside the GTM container (see docs/analytics-and-seo.md).
NEXT_PUBLIC_GTM_ID=

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Enquiry delivery
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

# ENQUIRY_WEBHOOK_URL — HTTPS endpoint that receives each enquiry as JSON (POST).
#   Optional. Server only. When unset, the form validates but tells the visitor that
#   nothing was sent. Must be https (http is accepted only for localhost).
#   Get it from: the receiving service (serverless function, Zapier/Make/n8n webhook…).
ENQUIRY_WEBHOOK_URL=

# ENQUIRY_WEBHOOK_SECRET — optional token sent as `Authorization: Bearer <value>`.
#   SECRET. Server only. Never prefix with NEXT_PUBLIC_.
ENQUIRY_WEBHOOK_SECRET=

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Asset generation (local scripts only — never used by the website at runtime)
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

# GEMINI_API_KEY — SECRET. Used only by scripts/generate-*.ts on your machine.
#   Never set it in the hosting provider unless you run those scripts there.
GEMINI_API_KEY=
IMAGE_GEN_MODEL_NAME=gemini-nano-banana-2.1
VIDEO_GEN_MODEL_NAME=gemini-omni-1.1-flash
